# Loading Patterns

## Decision Guide

| Context                    | Pattern              |
|----------------------------|----------------------|
| List / collection page     | Page skeleton        |
| Card / sidebar content     | `Skeleton`           |
| Button action in-progress  | `Button loading` prop |
| Inline expand / fetch      | `Spinner`            |
| Form page loading          | Full-page spinner    |

## Button Loading

Always use the built-in `loading` prop when the shared `Button` supports it — never manually render spinners inside the button:

```tsx
<Button loading={isPending}>Save</Button>
```

If `Button` does not yet have `loading`, add it to the primitive instead of one-off spinners at call sites.

## Route `loading.tsx`

Prefer a skeleton that matches the page layout (product landing, cart, checkout). Keep the fallback visually close to the final UI so it does not jump.

## Collection / refetch states

- **Initial load** (no data): full skeleton
- **Refetch** (data exists): keep content visible with reduced opacity overlay
- **Error**: centered message, no spinner
